    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42376" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salsāmentum</span></b> , i, n.
		salsus. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Fish-pickle</i>, <i>brine</i>,
			* <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 2, 57, 117</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Salted</i> or <i>pickled fish</i>
			(usu. in plur.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salsamenta Fac macerentur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Ad. 3, 3, 26</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 17, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 8,
				17, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 2, 9, § 18</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">32, 7, 26, §
				79</span></i>; <i><span class="en">32, 9,
				34, § 106 al.</span></i>—<i>Sing.</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 12, 55, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 2,
				24, 7</span></i>.</div>
